= Ürgüplü Meets with İbrahim Öktem

As Ürgüplü continues his efforts to form a new government, CHP Party Assembly member İbrahim Öktem requests a meeting with the prospective Prime Minister. Having previously discussed the situation with CHP Secretary General Kâmil Kırıkoğlu and Bülent Ecevit, Öktem arrives to communicate their views on resolving the government crisis and securing CHP's participation. During their conversation, Öktem emphasizes the importance of carrying out the reforms promised following the March 12 Memorandum, arguing that the military's honor and reputation can only be preserved through a government genuinely committed to reform rather than another unsuccessful administration.

Öktem also stresses the importance of appointing ministers capable of implementing these reforms, warning Ürgüplü against repeating the mistakes of Erim's previous governments. However, selecting CHP ministers presents another difficulty, as the party remains deeply divided between the supporters of Ecevit and İnönü. Ürgüplü expresses confidence that he can find suitable candidates acceptable to both factions, hoping to secure CHP's cooperation without bringing its internal disputes into his proposed cabinet. For now, the meeting ends on a positive note, with both sides expressing their desire to see the government crisis resolved.

